  "progression": "Volume increases by ~1 set per muscle group per week (MEV→MAV over 4 weeks). Load increases when RPE is below target (add weight if RPE 7 feels like 6). Deload at week 4 by cutting volume ~50%. Repeat mesocycle with slightly higher MEV starting point.",
  "notes": "RP-style programming is RPE-driven — if the prescribed RPE isn't being hit, you must add weight. Never use the same weight for 4 straight weeks just to 'finish the plan.' Adaptations require progressive overload."
